          "path": "_m/s/x/k/9/church-mosque-of-vefa-wp/see-wikimedia-article.jpg",
          "filename": "Molla Gurani mosque 1338.jpg",
          "caption": "See the Wikimedia article for an explanation. During several visits in the 2010's the neighbourhood surrounding is was being torn down, after which \"new old houses\" would be built. I saw an example: the by now usual wooden building with possibly inside a concrete structure (the people told me here only wood would be used, I could not check). During my latest visit (December 2018) it seemed the mosque was being restored. It stood forlorn in a sea of torn down houses (some remained, to be restored, some were inhabited by the poorest of people).",
